Subject: [PATCH] wineandroid.drv: Don't send a second left button down for mouse clicks.

Android delivers a mouse click as ACTION_DOWN and ACTION_BUTTON_PRESS with
the same button state. The second event added no new button, so it was
taken for a touch event and sent another left button down, which Wine
turned into a double click: a single click on a game in Steam's library
started it (or opened the install dialog).

Only treat ACTION_DOWN without any button pressed as a touch.
---
--- a/dlls/wineandroid.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/wineandroid.drv/window.c
@@ -301,7 +301,10 @@
             data.motion.input.mi.dwFlags |= MOUSEEVENTF_RIGHTDOWN;
         if ((state & ~prev_state) & AMOTION_EVENT_BUTTON_TERTIARY)
             data.motion.input.mi.dwFlags |= MOUSEEVENTF_MIDDLEDOWN;
-        if (!(state & ~prev_state)) /* touch event */
+        /* touch event; a mouse click comes as ACTION_DOWN and ACTION_BUTTON_PRESS with
+         * the same button state, and a second left down for the latter made Wine see a
+         * double click (Steam's library started games on a single click) */
+        if (mask == AMOTION_EVENT_ACTION_DOWN && !(state & 0x7fffffff))
             data.motion.input.mi.dwFlags |= MOUSEEVENTF_LEFTDOWN;
         break;
     case AMOTION_EVENT_ACTION_UP:
